# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Benchmark results (`make bench`): they describe one machine
/bench/

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Lock files of the package managers the website does not use. web/ is pnpm,
# and its pnpm-lock.yaml is committed: CI installs with --frozen-lockfile and
# Vercel installs from it, so dependency versions never drift between them.
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpmfile.js

# Editor directories and files
.idea
.vscode
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Build output (make build / make links, GoReleaser)
bin/
dist/
completions/

# The binary belongs in bin/ (make build) and is run from there. A bare
# `go build` at the root drops it here instead; it must never be committed.
/gnux
/gnux.exe

# The playground's WebAssembly build (make web/wasm); rebuilt, never committed
web/public/gnux.wasm
web/public/wasm_exec.js

# The generated reference (make docs, go generate ./...): rebuilt from the
# tool registry whenever it is needed, never committed. The man pages are
# generated for the release archives, the MDX before every website build.
# Only the hand-written guides (documentation/guides) and the snapshots of
# released docs (web/content/docs/vX.Y, written by tools/docsnap) are kept.
/documentation/man/
/documentation/markdown/
/documentation/rest/
/documentation/yaml/
/web/content/docs/*
!/web/content/docs/v[0-9]*/
/web/public/reference/
